SIM-01: fix the sign in the "tank empty within the next second" test

tanklevels() snaps a tank to Vmax or Vmin when it would reach that volume
within the next second. NodeDemand is the tank's net inflow, which is
negative while it drains, so the empty test must add it, the same way the
full test does. With the minus sign the test only fired once the tank was
already more than a second's flow below Vmin.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply SIM-01_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..58aaefe 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -1083,7 +1083,7 @@ void  tanklevels(Project *pr, long tstep)
         {
             tank->V = tank->Vmax;
         }
-        else if (tank->V - hyd->NodeDemand[n] <= tank->Vmin)
+        else if (tank->V + hyd->NodeDemand[n] <= tank->Vmin)
         {
             tank->V = tank->Vmin;
         }
